armland-atlas/kansas/reno-county"],["ARC or PLC in Reno County","/arc-plc/kansas/reno-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Reno County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids, February to March came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years, and in 2025 it came in at 23%. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 35% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21128 had its driest year in 1956, at 40% of normal.</p>"}
